# The ledger of `web/steps`: the middleware Echo's `middleware` package, Gin
# and chi ship ready for a router's chain, one block per capability, and what
# Rebel answers as a step of `web/chain`. Each is made of a piece of `web`,
# whose ledger holds the piece's own block. Rust's standard library holds no
# web framework, and Python's none of these steps, so their lines are `-`.

capability steps/log  a line for each request, with its status and the time it took
  heroes  web/steps.access_log
  go      echo/middleware.Logger, echo/middleware.LoggerWithConfig, echo/middleware.RequestLoggerWithConfig, gin.Logger, chi/middleware.Logger
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    the time is read twice from a clock the program hands it, called with the program's state, so a test advances its own; the line's time is the logger's; a failure handed on is written at `error` with its code, where Echo's logger writes the error its handler answers

capability steps/request-id  an identifier for each request, kept where the client sent one, copied into the response
  heroes  web/steps.request_id
  go      echo/middleware.RequestID, echo/middleware.RequestIDWithConfig, chi/middleware.RequestID
  rust    -
  python  -

capability steps/cors  cross-origin requests allowed by origin, a preflight answered before the handler
  heroes  web/steps.cors
  go      echo/middleware.CORS, echo/middleware.CORSWithConfig, go-chi/cors.Handler
  rust    -
  python  -

capability steps/basic-auth  a request refused 401 without credentials the program accepts, checked against its own state
  heroes  web/steps.basic_auth
  go      echo/middleware.BasicAuth, echo/middleware.BasicAuthWithConfig, gin.BasicAuth, chi/middleware.BasicAuth
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    the check is called with the program's state by `@`, so it reads the program's accounts and may count a refusal, where Echo's validator closes over them

capability steps/body-limit  a body past a size refused 413 before the handler
  heroes  web/steps.body_limit
  go      echo/middleware.BodyLimit, echo/middleware.BodyLimitWithConfig, chi/middleware.RequestSize
  rust    -
  python  -

capability steps/secure  the security headers on every response
  heroes  web/steps.security_headers
  go      echo/middleware.Secure, echo/middleware.SecureWithConfig
  rust    -
  python  -

capability steps/gzip  a response compressed by gzip where the client accepts it
  heroes  web/steps.gzip
  go      echo/middleware.Gzip, echo/middleware.GzipWithConfig, chi/middleware.Compress
  rust    -
  python  -

capability steps/timeout  a handler stopped past a time
  heroes  refused: a handler runs to its end on the thread that serves, and the language has no way to stop a function midway, so a step could answer late but never stop the work, and `web` offers no deadline a handler reads; `http.Server.deadline_ms` bounds a connection instead
  go      echo/middleware.Timeout, echo/middleware.TimeoutWithConfig, echo/middleware.ContextTimeout, chi/middleware.Timeout
  rust    -
  python  -

capability steps/rate-limit  requests of one client counted and refused 429 past a rate
  heroes  web.limit_rate
  go      echo/middleware.RateLimiter, echo/middleware.RateLimiterWithConfig
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    called by a step of the program's own with the limiter its state holds, since no step generic over a state reaches a field of it

dropped  a skipper deciding per request whether a step runs: a step of the program's own decides before calling one of these, or calls its `go_on` straight away
